  "nl_text": "The database name is rschema_0066, and it contains four tables: community, owner, house, and repair_application_record. The community table has columns for community_id, community_name, address, and manager, with community_id being the primary key. The owner table has columns for owner_id, name, phone, house_number, and community_id, with owner_id being the primary key and community_id being a foreign key referencing the community table. The house table has columns for house_id, house_name, and location, with house_id being the primary key. The repair_application_record table has columns for owner_id, house_id, application_time, repair_content, and repair_cost, with a composite primary key of (house_id, owner_id) and foreign keys referencing the owner and house tables.",
  "gold_question": "Description of customer management business requirements of a property management company:\n\nA property management company manages multiple communities, each of which has multiple owners. The owner has a name, phone number, and house number. The property management company needs to record the owner's maintenance application, and each maintenance application needs to record the application time, maintenance content, and maintenance cost. The company needs to count the maintenance costs of each community for performance appraisal.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0066.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0066\nCREATE TABLE `community` (\n  `community_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `community_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `manager` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`community_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `owner` (\n  `owner_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `phone` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `house_number` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `community_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`owner_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `owner_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`community_id`) REFERENCES `community` (`community_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `house` (\n  `house_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `house_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `location` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`house_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `repair_application_record` (\n  `owner_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `house_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `application_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `repair_content` text NOT NULL,\n  `repair_cost` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`house_id`, `owner_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `repair_application_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`owner_id`) REFERENCES `owner` (`owner_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `repair_application_record_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`house_id`) REFERENCES `house` (`house_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
